DECISIONS 213, CODEGEN.md §2.1, §3.5: a go package defaulted from out is not validated by check yet, so a dependency's default that is no Go identifier stays E8011 at its importer.
-- b/b.canon --
package b

/// A colour.
enum Tone { red, blue }

emit go { out: "@features/1b" }
-- a/a.canon --
package a

import b { Tone }

/// A badge.
record Badge {
  /// Its colour.
  tone: Tone
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8011]  a/a.canon:11:6
  1b is not a valid go identifier for @go(name:)

1 error, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
